{"@context":"http://iiif.io/api/presentation/3/context.json","id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/manifests/science-fiction-a-case-study-of-starship-troopers.json","type":"Manifest","label":{"en":["Science Fiction: A Case Study of Starship Troopers"]},"homepage":[{"id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling","type":"Text","label":{"en":["Science Fiction: A Case Study of Starship Troopers"]},"format":"text/html"}],"metadata":[{"label":{"en":["Description"]},"value":{"en":["Annotations by Xavier Beijerinck"]}},{"label":{"en":["Language"]},"value":{"en":["English"]}}],"items":[{"id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/science_fiction_a_case_study_of_starship_troopers/canvas/4","type":"Canvas","duration":3586,"annotations":[{"@context":"http://iiif.io/api/presentation/3/context.json","id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/manifests/science_fiction_a_case_study_of_starship_troopers-canvas4-1","type":"AnnotationPage","label":{"en":["Default"]},"items":[{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/science_fiction_a_case_study_of_starship_troopers/canvas/4/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Introduction","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Science Fiction","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Movie","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/science_fiction_a_case_study_of_starship_troopers/canvas/4#t=0,78"},{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/science_fiction_a_case_study_of_starship_troopers/canvas/4/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"The science fiction movie Starship Troopers directed by Paul Verhoeven is an adaptation of Starship Troopers by Robert A Heinlein. The movie is a satire of the militarism of America and fascism which is evidenced by the director's commentary. ","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Science Fiction","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Movie","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Politics","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Futuristic","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/science_fiction_a_case_study_of_starship_troopers/canvas/4#t=80,360"},{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/science_fiction_a_case_study_of_starship_troopers/canvas/4/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"The protagonist of Starship Troopers, Johny Rico, is a white man from Argentina. Casper Van Dein talks about how Johny Rico was the descendant of Nazis who fled to Argentina after the Second World War.","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Science Fiction","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Movie","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Politics","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/science_fiction_a_case_study_of_starship_troopers/canvas/4#t=361,440"},{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/science_fiction_a_case_study_of_starship_troopers/canvas/4/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"The note of Mormon extremism is a direct reference to American history through this detail of the world-building as a direct critique of America's colonial past. ","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Science Fiction","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Movie","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Politics","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Dystopian","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/science_fiction_a_case_study_of_starship_troopers/canvas/4#t=440,540"},{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/science_fiction_a_case_study_of_starship_troopers/canvas/4/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"The shower scene satirises the policies and positions of America's past, particularly the exclusion of rights from groups of people, and the way the military recruits vulnerable people by offering to pay for their college tuition in exchange for military service. ","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Science Fiction","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Movie","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Politics","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Dystopian","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Futuristic","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/science_fiction_a_case_study_of_starship_troopers/canvas/4#t=541,600"},{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/science_fiction_a_case_study_of_starship_troopers/canvas/4/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"The speech given by the Sky Marshall  parodies overly militaristic language and warmongering. ","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Science Fiction","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Movie","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Politics","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Dystopian","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/science_fiction_a_case_study_of_starship_troopers/canvas/4#t=601,640"},{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/science_fiction_a_case_study_of_starship_troopers/canvas/4/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"This is the beginning of the section of the video that focuses upon the book Starship Troopers, as opposed to the movie. ","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Science Fiction","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Movie","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Politics","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Dystopian","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/science_fiction_a_case_study_of_starship_troopers/canvas/4#t=1060,1070"},{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/science_fiction_a_case_study_of_starship_troopers/canvas/4/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"The book is being explained in chronological order for narrative sense as the book starts with the protagonist Juan Rico assaulting an alien civilisation in order to cause property damage. One of the first canonical scenes is a moral philosophy lesson undertaken by Juan, where Heinlein makes an argument against Marxist philosophy.","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Science Fiction","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Television Show","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Politics","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Futuristic","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Dystopian","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/science_fiction_a_case_study_of_starship_troopers/canvas/4#t=1071,1370"},{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/science_fiction_a_case_study_of_starship_troopers/canvas/4/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"As Juan is in training during a low point, he gets a message from his philosophy teacher who attempts to console Juan. This consolation is another philosophical scream against Marxist philosophy, which at the time that Heinlein was writing, was perceived as the cultural and political enemy of America, free market capitalism, and libertarianism which were ideals Heinlein believed in.","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Science Fiction","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Movie","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Politics","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Futuristic","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Dystopian","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/science_fiction_a_case_study_of_starship_troopers/canvas/4#t=1371,1530"},{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/science_fiction_a_case_study_of_starship_troopers/canvas/4/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Heinlein uses the setting and genre of Starship Troopers to critique the as he saw it growing weakness within American culture. Heinlein presents a world that only though strength and military might can survive an existential threat. The 'bugs'  are a thinly disguised analogy for Communism and China.","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Science Fiction","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Movie","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Politics","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Futuristic","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/science_fiction_a_case_study_of_starship_troopers/canvas/4#t=0,0"},{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/science_fiction_a_case_study_of_starship_troopers/canvas/4/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Heinlein uses the setting and genre of Starship Troopers to critique the growing weakness he saw within American culture. Heinlein presents a world that will only survive an existential threat through strength and military might. The 'bugs' which are a thinly disguised analogy to Communism and China.","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Science Fiction","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Movie","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Politics","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Futuristic","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Dystopian","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/science_fiction_a_case_study_of_starship_troopers/canvas/4#t=1531,2100"}]}],"items":[{"id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/science_fiction_a_case_study_of_starship_troopers-canvas4/paintings","type":"AnnotationPage","items":[{"id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/science_fiction_a_case_study_of_starship_troopers-canvas4/paintings","type":"Annotation","motivation":"painting","body":{"id":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JSg6eOmgvW8&t=178s","type":"Video","format":"unknown","duration":3586},"target":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/science_fiction_a_case_study_of_starship_troopers/canvas/4"}]}]}]}